  "headline": "Digoxin is not on FDA's current shortage list; an earlier shortage was first posted 2021-06-04 and is resolved",
  "headline_cites": ["D11"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's records show digoxin is not on the current shortage list as of 2026-10-21; the prior shortage was first posted 2021-06-04 and has since been resolved.",
      "cites": ["D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1110509 at Bryant Ranch PrePack ended 2019-11-18 and was classified VAI, 564 days before the 2021-06-04 posting.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1125050 at Hikma Farmaceutica (Portugal) S.A. ended 2020-03-06 and was classified VAI, 455 days before the 2021-06-04 posting.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsequent inspections at both plants remained VAI after the posting, with no OAI classification recorded before the shortage was posted.",
      "cites": ["D8", "D9", "D10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 79 units of the 0.25 mg/mL 2 mL injection with 6.1 days on hand; Corvale General holds 199 units with 14.5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 6 units of the 0.25 mg/mL 2 mL injection from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave Corvale General with 14 days and bring Corvale East to 7 days.",
      "cites": ["D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternate sourcing from Covis Pharma US, Inc. (plant AZURITY) and an alternate concentration from Sandoz Inc. (250 mcg/mL) are also available per P&T interchange approvals.",
      "cites": ["D13", "D14"]
    }
  ]
}
